    "turns": [
        {
            "role": "A",
            "text": "Behind the technical name Actor-Critic, what intuitive problem were researchers confronting?",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial-hook"
        },
        {
            "role": "B",
            "text": "Actor-critic methods split reinforcement learning into a policy component that acts and a value component that evaluates. This architecture made it possible to improve behavior using learned criticism rather than waiting for full returns.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-neuronlike-adaptive-elements-that-can-solve-difficult-learning-control-problems"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-legacy-achievement-summary", "claim-legacy-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.historical-background"
        },
        {
            "role": "A",
            "text": "That sounds like a promising direction. What mechanism actually makes it work?",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial"
        },
        {
            "role": "B",
            "text": "The actor chooses an action, the critic estimates whether the outcome was better than expected, and the actor shifts future choices accordingly.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-neuronlike-adaptive-elements-that-can-solve-difficult-learning-control-problems"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-legacy-achievement-summary", "claim-legacy-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.core-idea"
        },
        {
            "role": "A",
            "text": "Why did the idea outlive one paper or experiment? What did later researchers actually inherit?",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial"
        },
        {
            "role": "B",
            "text": "Experts generally treat actor-critic as a core architecture for modern reinforcement learning. Its long-term legacy is the policy-value split that underlies A3C, DDPG, PPO-style training, and many game or robotics agents.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-neuronlike-adaptive-elements-that-can-solve-difficult-learning-control-problems"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-legacy-achievement-summary", "claim-legacy-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.long-term-legacy"
        },
        {
            "role": "SUMMARY",
            "text": "Actor-Critic mattered not only as a result, but as a method that later researchers could test, adapt, and extend.",
